ties of daily living to seniors who are independent or who require some support. The company operates home health, hospice, and home care agencies, as well as senior living communities in Alabama, Arizona, California, Colorado, Idaho, Montana, Nevada, Oklahoma, Oregon, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Washington, Wisconsin, and Wyoming. The Company was incorporated in 2019 and is headquartered in Eagle, Idaho.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brent J. Guerisoli | CEO & Chairman | Age 44 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $98K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 19%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $4K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $922 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 22\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["The Pennant Group, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.3B market cap on $948M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +26% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $36M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.63\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 7.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 37% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3726186632224733},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Did Strong Q3 Earnings Just Shift Pennant Group (PNTG) Investment Narrative?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-pntg/pennant-group/news/did-strong-q3-earnings-just-shift-pennant-group-pntg-investm","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794579635.692,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(PNTG) Volatility Zones as Tactical Triggers","sou